'' A DELETED VENDOR DLL COMES BACK ON THE NEXT BUILD (RFC-0002 V13): the copy runs after the
'' link step, not inside it -- which an unchanged program's build may skip -- so a second
'' build of the same project puts the DLL back beside the program, and copy_to copies it again.
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' ENV: TKO_PKG=build/.vcu/pkg
'' ENV: TKO_MODCACHE=build/.vcu/mc
'' CLEAN: build/.vcu
'' COPY: tests/modules/src/vlink/pkg => build/.vcu/pkg
'' STEP: -target windows-x86_64 -dll tests/modules/src/vlink/libsrc/alpha_dynamic.tiko -o build/.vcu/pkg/vendor/alpha/lib/alpha_windows_x86_64.dll
'' COPY: tests/modules/src/vlink/proj => build/.vcu/proj
'' STEP: build -target windows-x86_64 --manifest build/.vcu/proj
'' CLEAN: build/.vcu/proj/out/debug/alpha_windows_x86_64.dll
'' CLEAN: build/.vcu/proj/dist
'' ARGS: build -target windows-x86_64 --manifest build/.vcu/proj
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: build/.vcu/proj/out/debug/alpha_windows_x86_64.dll
'' EXPECT-FILE: build/.vcu/proj/dist/alpha_windows_x86_64.dll
'' RUN: build/.vcu/proj/out/debug/app.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  2             alpha header: dynamic
